### 🔴 First attempt: authentication SUCCEEDED and the session still failed

The first run of the positive leg used a server whose Access-Accept carried only a
Reply-Message. Result on the console:

    awplus login: radclient1
    Password:
    login:
    Session setup problem, abort.

The server log proves this was **not** an authentication failure:

    09:22:50 Access-Request  from 10.38.22.34 id=195 user='radclient1' | Message-Authenticator=0x451a...,
             User-Name='radclient1', User-Password=<hidden>, NAS-Identifier='console',
             NAS-Port=20833, NAS-Port-Type=5, Service-Type=8(Authenticate-Only)
    09:22:50 Access-Accept   to 10.38.22.34 id=195 user='radclient1' (ok)

and the DUT's own log names the cause:

    2026 Oct 19 20:22:36 authpriv.err awplus login: Invalid user name "radclient1". Abort.
    2026 Oct 19 20:22:41 daemon.notice awplus systemd[1]: serial-getty@ttyS0.service: Main process exited, code=exited, status=1/FAILURE

**An Access-Accept with no authorization attributes is accepted and then discarded.** Adding
`Service-Type = Administrative (6)` and the Cisco-style VSA `shell:priv-lvl=15` to the Accept
made the identical login succeed (STEP 5). This is an instrument defect of the first server
configuration, not a DUT defect -- but the behaviour is worth recording, because the console
message "Session setup problem, abort." gives no hint that the missing thing is an
authorization attribute in the RADIUS reply.

STEP 4 verdict: PASS (configuration applied and visible; the first Accept was corrected).
`<dev>.cfg` saved at this point: T33408/swi_d.cfg (102 config lines).

