A manager session opened before accounting was turned on still produced a Stop
(`Acct-Session-Time=47`) when it ended -- the DUT accounts the end of a session it did not
account the start of.

STEP 5 verdict: PASS, at frame level, with three independent views agreeing (console outcome,
server log, wire capture).

### A DUT-side discriminator for "who authenticated this login": the `Last login:` line

Spotted by the sentinel in the console feed, then CONFIRMED here against the server log,
which is the only thing that can settle it. From work/banner-grep.txt, across this case:

| console login | authenticated by (server log) | banner |
| --- | --- | --- |
| manager 09:19, 09:21, 09:25 | local (no server configured / method list local) | `Last login: … on ttyS0` present |
| manager 09:24:21, 09:28:5x, 09:29:5x | local fallback (server unreachable) | `Last login: …` present |
| radclient1 09:26:26 | RADIUS Access-Accept | **no `Last login:` line** |
| manager 09:26:29, 09:27:29 | RADIUS Access-Accept | **no `Last login:` line** |

Five local logins print it, three RADIUS-served logins do not, no exceptions. The mechanism is
plain: `Last login:` comes from the Linux lastlog of a local account, and a RADIUS-authenticated
session has no local account to read it from. **This is a discriminator visible on the DUT
console alone**, and it is worth adding to `platforms/x960.md`. It is offered as a
corroborating observation; the authoritative instruments remain the server log and the wire.

